NorwayNumberingTitle=Number sequences
NorwayNumberingModelInfo=Short consecutive invoice, credit note and proposal references. Choose prefixes and starting numbers in Norwegian setup → Number sequences.
NorwayNumberingScope=Invoices, credit notes and proposals receive separate increasing six-digit sequences, without separators or year/month components. Customers and suppliers each receive a five-digit sequence starting at 00001, without letters. Defaults are F000001, K000001 and T000001. The sequence does not reset at a new year. Existing references are retained.
NorwayNumberingPayments=Repayment is recorded as a payment against the invoice. The invoice retains its reference.
NorwayNumberingSaved=Numbering saved. The next number is assigned automatically when issuing a document.
NorwayNumberingFailed=Unable to read or save numbering. Review formats and existing sequences. Changed source data requires a new preview. Settings are locked after a new document is issued. Custom numbering modules or the same prefix with a different digit width require separate review.
NorwayNumberingActive=The selected number sequences are active.
NorwayNumberingNotActive=The proposal is not active yet. Current numbering remains until confirmed saving.
NorwayNumberingLocked=New documents have been issued since configuration. Prefixes and starting numbers are locked to preserve the sequence. Numbering continues automatically.
NorwayNumberingNext=Next reference
NorwayNumberingNotReserved=References are previews and are not reserved. Another user may issue a document first.
