NorwayReconcileTitle=Invoice amount against posted gross totals
NorwayReconcileScope=Limited read-only control for an ordinary NOK invoice or credit note with one voucher. Compares debit and credit totals with the absolute invoice amount including VAT; invoice total comparisons allow one øre difference, while debit and credit must be exactly equal. References and date are also checked. Customer, sales and VAT account allocation, payments, fees, reversals and complete posting are not reconciled. Current data is read on demand; refresh after concurrent changes.
NorwayReconcileMatch=Gross totals agree within the scope of this control. Account allocation and VAT treatment are not confirmed.
NorwayReconcileDifferent=Difference in gross totals or balance.
NorwayReconcileReview=The data requires review before gross totals can be assessed.
NorwayReconcileEmpty=No linked ledger entries. No reconciliation was performed.
NorwayReconcileUnavailable=Gross totals could not be checked. Unsupported or incomplete data, truncation or a read error may be the cause.
NorwayReconcileGross=Absolute invoice amount including VAT
NorwayReconcileDebit=Posted debit
NorwayReconcileCredit=Posted credit
NorwayReconcileDifference=Debit minus credit
NorwayStandardTitle=Norwegian default accounts under Accounting
NorwayStandardScope=The overview covers all 46 default-account fields in the supported Dolibarr version, including optional features. Select only accounts suitable for their purpose. No account is selected automatically. Preview and confirmation only fill empty choices in a new accounting setup with the bundled Norwegian chart. Existing choices remain. History, changed accounts or an unsuitable chart block filling. These are fallback accounts; product, service, customer and tax-rate mappings may override them. Rates, deduction rights and VAT status remain unchanged.
NorwayStandardField=Default account and purpose
NorwayStandardCurrent=Current choice
NorwayStandardChoice=Choose a proposal
NorwayStandardNoChange=Leave unchanged
NorwayStandardSeparate=Review separately if the feature is used
NorwayStandardPreview=Preview selected mappings
NorwayStandardSave=Confirm filling empty default accounts
NorwayStandardConfirmScope=I have reviewed the purposes, VAT assumptions and selected accounts, and have a recent backup. Only empty choices should be filled.
NorwayStandardReasonCustomer=Customer receivables. Customer-specific mappings may override.
NorwayStandardReasonSupplier=Supplier payables. Supplier-specific mappings may override.
NorwayStandardReasonSalary=Only for employees and ordinary salary payables; not owner withdrawals in a sole proprietorship.
NorwayStandardReasonExpense=Employee expenses to reimburse. Sole proprietor expenses require separate consideration.
NorwayStandardReasonDomesticSale=Domestic standard-rate taxable sales for a VAT-registered entity. Other rates or exempt supplies need separate mappings.
NorwayStandardReasonGoodsBuy=Choose raw materials (4000/4030), goods under manufacture (4100) or finished goods for resale (4300/4330), and the applicable rate. Fixed assets and other purchases require their own accounts; assess capitalisation separately.
NorwayStandardReasonServiceBuy=Choose by expense type, such as subcontracting, rental, accounting/audit, advice, advertising or IT. In this chart 4500/4550 and 6790/6795 distinguish reporting obligations. 6420 is IT rental, 6552 acquisition and 6553 annual maintenance. Assess reporting obligations, accruals and capitalisation separately. One default does not suit every service.
NorwayStandardReasonIntra=Core field for trade between EU countries. Norway is outside the EU VAT area; this is not a general account for European purchases or sales.
NorwayStandardReasonForeign=Foreign trade requires the supply, country and customer type to be established. Zero-rated and exempt treatments differ; no general mapping is assigned.
NorwayStandardReasonVatSOLD=Fallback standard-rate output VAT account, not a rate or tax code.
NorwayStandardReasonVatBUY=Fallback standard-rate input VAT account. Deduction eligibility is separate.
NorwayStandardReasonVatPAY=VAT settlement account for payments/refunds. Does not replace a VAT return or reconciliation.
NorwayStandardReasonLocalTax=Core local tax 1/2 is not Norwegian VAT. Leave empty without a specifically qualified need.
NorwayStandardReasonReverse=Reverse-charge accounts depend on purchase type and rate. Do not assign generally before the scenario is established.
NorwayStandardReasonTransfer=Requires a suitable clearing account for transfers between bank accounts. The bank account 1920 is not automatically the correct clearing account.
NorwayStandardReasonWarranty=Retained warranty requires a qualified contract and receivable account.
NorwayStandardReasonDonation=Gifts, grants and donations are classified by substance and legal form.
NorwayStandardReasonMembership=Membership fees require the legal form and tax treatment to be established.
NorwayStandardReasonLoanCapital=2220 is debt to credit institutions. Owner loans and other borrowing use separate accounts.
NorwayStandardReasonLoanInterest=8150 is bank-loan interest expense, not principal repayments or every fee.
NorwayStandardReasonLoanInsurance=7500 is insurance premiums. Loan fees must not be treated as insurance here.
NorwayStandardReasonSuspense=Unidentified receipts and payments require a suitable clearing account and follow-up. Bank, income and expense accounts are not chosen automatically.
NorwayStandardReasonDiscount=Financial payment discounts and price reductions differ. Check core usage and tax impact before selecting an account.
NorwayStandardReasonCustomerDeposit=2900 is a customer advance liability. Advance invoicing and VAT timing require separate consideration.
NorwayStandardReasonDepositVat=Technical customer-deposit VAT mapping. Requires a qualified advance workflow; not ordinary VAT settlement.
NorwayStandardReasonSupplierDeposit=1480 is for goods contracts/projects; 1749 is prepaid operating expenses. Choose by the payment purpose.
