NorwayStandardReasonGoodsSale=Choose by traded/manufactured goods and tax treatment. High/medium rates, domestic zero rating and exemption have different accounts. One default does not automatically distinguish multiple kinds of sale.
NorwayStandardReasonServiceSale=Choose by the service tax treatment: high or low rate, domestic zero rating or exemption. In this chart 3120 is domestic zero-rated sales; qualifying exports use 3125.
NorwayStandardReasonForeignGoodsSale=3105 covers exports of traded goods and 3115 manufactured goods when export zero rating is documented. A foreign customer alone does not establish zero rating. Other treatments require item codes or separate setup. The account does not set the VAT rate.
NorwayStandardReasonForeignServiceSale=In this chart 3125 covers exported services qualifying for Norwegian VAT zero rating after assessment of the supply and recipient. Do not use it as a universal zero rate for foreign customers. Other treatments require individual service codes or separate setup.
NorwayStandardReasonForeignGoodsBuy=4040/4041/4042 cover foreign raw-material purchases and 4340/4341/4342 goods for resale, split by high/medium rate or zero rating. Numbers follow the bundled chart. Customs evidence, import basis and import VAT require separate handling.
NorwayStandardReasonForeignServiceBuy=Choose the expense type as for domestic service purchases. Supplier country alone does not determine the expense account. Remotely supplied services may require reverse charge; deduction rights and Norwegian/foreign VAT must be assessed separately. This choice does not calculate or report import VAT.
NorwayStandardGroupForeign=Exports and imports
