NorwayVatAccountsTitle=Fill VAT accounts for sales and purchases
NorwayVatAccountsScope=Preview empty account fields on active ordinary Norwegian VAT rows without a special code: 25% → 2700/2710, 15% → 2701/2711 and 12% → 2703/2713 (sales/purchases) in the shipped chart. Requires an unused setup without validated invoices or ledger history. Existing choices are preserved. Default accounts and rate accounts are separate settings; saving defaults does not fill these fields.
NorwayVatAccountsSeparate=No rates are created, activated or changed. Historical rates such as 8 and 14%, zero rates, coded and special rows, imports and reverse charge require separate review. Accounts do not determine registration, deduction rights, tax treatment or reporting.
NorwayVatAccountsConfirm=I confirm that rows to fill concern ordinary domestic taxable sales/purchases and that the displayed accounts are correct. Deduction rights and the correct rate must be assessed for each transaction.
NorwayWizardTaskVatAccounts=Fill sales and purchase accounts on VAT rates
NorwayWizardTaskVatAccountsHelp=Default accounts do not fill the rate rows. Preview ordinary Norwegian rate accounts and confirm only in an unused accounting setup. Existing choices and special cases are preserved.

NorwayTaxAccountsTitle=Tax accounts – what needs setup?
NorwayTaxAccountsHelp=Tax accounts under Accounting map tax and contribution types to accounts for the Dolibarr tax/contribution module. This list is separate from the chart, VAT accounts and local taxes 1/2. An empty list does not mean the chart lacks tax accounts. Leave the list unchanged if this feature is not used.
NorwayTaxAccountsEnk=Sole proprietorship without employees: This list needs no entries for ordinary invoicing. Personal advance income tax paid from the business bank account is normally recorded using 2070 Forskuddsskatt in the shipped chart. The payment does not reduce business profit. An account alone creates no payment or ledger entry.
NorwayTaxAccountsOther=Other legal forms and businesses with employees: Establish the applicable taxes and contributions before creating mappings. Do not apply 2070 to every legal form. Norwegian tax calculation, payroll and reporting are not qualified by this guide. Existing types and mappings are preserved.
NorwayTaxAccountsOpen=Open Tax accounts in Dolibarr
NorwayTaxAccountsGuide=Read the tax account guide
NorwayWizardExtraTaxAccounts=Guide: Tax accounts
NorwayWizardExtraTaxAccountsHelp=Explains when the list can remain unchanged, the distinction from VAT accounts and tax accounts for sole proprietorships. Changes no settings.

NorwayVatRatesTitle=Set up ordinary Norwegian VAT rates
NorwayVatRatesScope=For an unused accounting setup with the shipped Norwegian chart: Create missing ordinary 25, 15 and 12% sales/purchase rates and deactivate ordinary unused 8 and 14% after confirmation. Existing rates, account codes and defaults are not overwritten. 0% is preserved.
NorwayVatRatesLimits=Rates alone do not select tax treatment. Exemptions, registration periods, deductions and imports require separate assessment. Historical document rates are unchanged. Fill the rate accounts separately after this setup.
NorwayVatRatesConfirm=I confirm that this is an unused accounting setup without documents or ledger history and that the displayed changes are correct. No invoice lines or VAT registration status change.
NorwayVatRatesCreate=Create ordinary sales/purchase rate
NorwayVatRatesDeactivate=Deactivate old ordinary rate; retain its row
NorwayVatRatesKeep=Preserve active ordinary rate and account choices
NorwayVatRatesReview=Existing rate or special choice requires manual review
NorwayVatRatesBlocked=Changes cannot be confirmed. Check the selected active Norwegian chart. Documents (including drafts/quotes/orders), ledger history, products with 8/14%, inactive or special rate rows and old default choices require manual review. No data changed.
NorwayVatRatesSource=Source: current Norwegian Tax Administration rates
NorwayWizardTaskVatRates=Set up ordinary Norwegian VAT rates
NorwayWizardTaskVatRatesHelp=For an unused setup: review 25/15/12 and old 8/14 before confirming. Documents, history and special choices block changes. Fill VAT accounts in the following task.

NorwayAllocationTitle=Posted customer, sales and VAT allocation
NorwayAllocationScope=Explicitly select an ordinary domestic profile from the shipped chart. Compare stored invoice net/VAT/gross with actual ledger entries on 1500, the displayed sales accounts and the rate VAT account. Positive amounts are debit, negative credit. A match applies only to this profile; it does not approve tax treatment, historical accounting choices or a VAT report. Current default-account settings are not used. Data is read on opening; refresh after concurrent changes.
